Say **“Smart Note this”** when something matters enough that you should not have to explain it again.

You should be able to click one GitHub link and immediately see:

- what was learned;
- why it matters;
- what it means in plain language;
- how Naya interprets it;
- how the machine represents it;
- where it sits in the Brain;
- what it connects to;
- how to use it;
- what is proven vs still uncertain;
- the exact Intelligent Block behind it.

The human should never have to inspect a JSON payload, workflow artifact, or database row just to understand what Naya saved.

My job is not to save words mechanically.

My job is to:

1. understand the human's intended meaning;
2. identify durable intelligence;
3. preserve provenance and privacy;
4. distill the meaning into one governed Intelligent Block;
5. reconcile exact duplicates and surface conflicts;
6. connect the intelligence to what it supports, refines, enables, contradicts, or depends on;
7. keep automatic capture at **CANDIDATE** until evidence warrants promotion;
8. register it in the common intelligence index;
9. make it contextually retrievable to future authorized Nayas;
10. create this human-readable Brain projection;
11. return the direct GitHub Smart Link;
12. later observe whether using it changes behavior/outcomes and learn only from verified results.

Awareness does **not** mean loading every Smart Note into every prompt. It means every authorized Naya knows how to find the right intelligence when the task makes it relevant.

The desired human experience becomes:

> **Say important things once.**

Benefits:

- less re-explaining;
- less lost intelligence;
- less manual filing;
- faster future Naya orientation;
- one clean Smart Link showing exactly what was retained;
- better privacy and authority control;
- relevant intelligence appears when needed rather than everything being dumped into context;
- decisions can build on proven lessons;
- successful patterns can compound;
- mistakes can become reusable learning;
- the Hub can eventually surface the same intelligence visually without creating a second brain.
